Z||000000||FieroJoe||01-01-2001||08:40 PM||||My driver's side power window motor really sucks.  It's much slower than the passenger's, and its louded, and generally crappier.  The car has 220,000 miles on it (you wouldnt think it had that many though), and the previous owner was a smoker, so I assume that the driver's side window received a lot of use.  Anyways, is there anything I can do to the motor, before I go ahead and replace it?<BR>   If I do need to replace it, anybody have a good one with low use for sale, as opposed to a $70 new one from the FieroStore?<P>Thanks for any info.<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||01-01-2001||09:14 PM||||swap connectors on the switches and make sure it's really the motor.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||01-01-2001||10:08 PM||||I'll definatly have to try that, but, if it wasnt that, what else is there that could be done?||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||01-02-2001||12:23 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroJoe:<BR><B>I'll definatly have to try that, but, if it wasnt that, what else is there that could be done?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>if its still slow, pull off interior panel, the grease they use on the windows is like the grease in the headlites, turns to putty. if it is clean all you can off and relube it with lithium grease. since your window does still work prob not a mechanical problem.also check for caked up grease in the tracks<P><p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 01-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroJoe||01-02-2001||12:50 PM||||Well I do know that it is the motor, not the switches.  Anyway, about the grease.....<P>    The motor is really loud, and struggles a lot (really bogs down) towards the end of rolling the window down.  Could this still be caused by the lack of grease, or hinderance of the old grease being in there?<BR>    I'll go back out there again soon and try that out.<BR>    Is it still possible that the motor is just dying?  I dont know the average life on them, I sure do hope that it is only the grease.||||reg||1
